6. Regulatory Alignment

This research is designed to align with emerging regulatory frameworks. The ARHA architecture provides a potential technical implementation of compute governance mandates, resolving the tension between insecure neoclouds and secure AI deployment.

· EU AI Act: Article 55's cybersecurity obligations for systemic-risk GPAI models can be operationalized through ARHA's attestation, tokenization, and monitoring stack. We engage with the European Commission's standardization request to CEN/CENELEC on AI and the draft CEN/CENELEC Joint Technical Committee 21 (AI) standards.
· NIST AI RMF: The "Govern" function is supported by the token-based quota system; "Map" by the threat model; "Measure" by the FSSL and MLEIS monitoring; and "Manage" by the emergency shutdown module. We also align with NIST AI 100-5 (draft) on secure AI development.

