Appendix H: Additional Proofs and Derivations

H.1 Conditional Leakage Bound Proof

By chain rule of mutual information:

I(\theta; \mathcal{O}_{\text{inf}}, \mathcal{O}_{\text{net}}, \mathcal{O}_{\text{side}}) = I(\theta; \mathcal{O}_{\text{inf}}) + I(\theta; \mathcal{O}_{\text{net}} | \mathcal{O}_{\text{inf}}) + I(\theta; \mathcal{O}_{\text{side}} | \mathcal{O}_{\text{inf}}, \mathcal{O}_{\text{net}})

Since conditioning reduces mutual information, we have the upper bound. Equality holds when channels are conditionally independent given θ.

H.2 Cumulative Exfiltration Probability Derivation (Revised)

Assume each interaction has independent detection failure probability p_FN,joint. Then probability of no failure in N interactions is (1 - p_FN,joint)^N. Hence ε_exfil = 1 - (1 - p_FN,joint)^N. The maximum N for a target ε_target is N_max = floor( log(1 - ε_target) / log(1 - p_FN,joint) ).

No specific numerical value is asserted until Phase 3 measurement. The architecture enforces N ≤ N_max via a counter.

H.3 DTCBF Synthesis Algorithm

```
Algorithm: DTCBF Synthesis via SOS
Input: dynamics f_q, disturbance set W, parameters α, γ1, γ2
Output: verified DTCBF h_q or failure

Steps:
1. Parameterize h_q(x) = σ_threshold - σ_j + γ1(C_min - c_t) + γ2(I_max - I_total,t)
2. Formulate SOS program: minimize 0 subject to
   h_q(f_q(x,u)+w) - (1-α)h_q(x) ≥ 0 for all x ∈ X, u ∈ U, w ∈ W
3. Apply S-procedure to convert universal quantifiers to SOS constraints
4. Solve using SOSTOOLS or YALMIP
5. If solution found, return h_q
6. Else try quadratic h_q; if fails, try higher-degree or data-driven
7. If all fail, return rule-based fallback
